pcbkit 1

// ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 (Espressif Systems): Wi-Fi 802.11b/g/n and Bluetooth LE 5 module,
// dual-core Xtensa LX7 240 MHz (ESP32-S3), 16 MB flash, 8 MB octal PSRAM, native USB, PCB antenna,
// 3.3 V
// Compiled from the part sheet `parts/ESP32_S3_WROOM_1.json` (`parts.create`); status: checked.
// Datasheet:
// https://www.espressif.com/sites/default/files/documentation/esp32-s3-wroom-1_wroom-1u_datasheet_en.pdf
// (v1.8)
// Pins: Espressif ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 & WROOM-1U datasheet v1.8, Table 3-1 Pin Definitions and Figure
// 3-1 Pin Layout; land pattern from Figures 10-1 and 11-1, positions cross-checked with
// Espressif's own footprint (espressif/kicad-libraries)
// Footprint: the datasheet's land pattern
// This file may be used, changed and shared without conditions, with the board or alone.

// Note: Supply: 3.0-3.6 V able to deliver 500 mA (Wi-Fi TX peaks); 22 uF (10 uF minimum) and 100
// nF at the 3V3 pin.
// Note: Strapping pins sampled at reset: IO0 (weak pull-up; low = download mode), IO46 (weak
// pull-down; keep low/floating), IO45 (weak pull-down; must stay low for the 3.3 V flash), IO3
// (JTAG source). Do not load them with circuits that pull the wrong way during reset.
// Note: N4R8/N8R8/N16R8 (octal PSRAM): IO35, IO36, IO37 are taken by the PSRAM; do not use them.
// R16V variants: IO47/IO48 are 1.8 V I/O.
// Note: Every free GPIO reaches UART, SPI, I2C, I2S, LEDC PWM, MCPWM, TWAI (CAN; needs an external
// transceiver), RMT and PCNT through the GPIO matrix; ADC2 is not usable while Wi-Fi runs, use
// ADC1 (IO1-IO10) for analog.
// Note: Antenna: the antenna area is the 6 mm at the top edge of the module (opposite the bottom
// pin row); no metal enclosure near it. The footprint keeps tracks, vias, pours and other parts
// out of the antenna area itself (the module's width plus 0.5 mm, and 0.5 mm beyond its edge), the
// minimum the datasheet marks as the keepout zone. The vendor's hardware design guidelines
// (Positioning a Module on a Base Board) strongly recommend the antenna outside the base board, or
// its feed point at the board edge with the board cut away beside and below it, and at least 15 mm
// of clearance around it in the product: place the module at a board edge with the antenna
// overhanging it (`place = [edge(.top, overhang = 6mm)]`: the rule's `overhang` is a Length, how
// far beyond the edge), keep copper and parts as far from the antenna as the board allows, and put
// ground copper with dense ground vias on the board near (not under) the antenna.
// Note: The EPAD (pin 41) to ground with thermal vias improves heat flow; use modest solder paste
// on it so the module does not float.

